  "name": "Conifur Northwest",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Conifur Northwest was an annual furry convention in the Seattle-Tacoma (SeaTac) area of Washington state, founded in 1998 by James \"Tibo\" Birdsall and chaired by Dan \"Flinthoof\" Canaan. It was a convention for fans and creators of anthropomorphic comics, books, movies and related media, aiming for an entertaining, informative, relaxing and inspirational weekend, and each year it chose one or two creative guests of honor. It ran from 1998 to 2005, held each fall in SeaTac, Fife and Tacoma, with attendance growing from 275 to over 520. From 2001 its charity auction supported the Washington State Ferret Rescue and Shelter. The convention was operated by a 501(c)(7) club of the same name, and its supplies were donated to All Fur Fun in 2007.",
